{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And they stood.</b> This teaches that He held the mountain over them like a cask, and said: If you accept the Torah, well and good; and if not, there shall be your burial. And there is a difficulty, for they said 'we will do and we will hear.' And one may answer: when the Holy One, blessed be He, sought to give the Torah to Israel, they said: How many Torahs do you have? He said to them: one in writing and one oral. They said: the written one we accept; the oral one we do not accept. Immediately He held the mountain over them like a cask, and it was stated in tractate Shabbat: from here is a great protest against the Torah, etc., as is said there. And further, it is in the Midrash: when the Holy One, blessed be He, gave the Torah to Israel, He wrapped a sword inside the Torah and said to them: if you accept the Torah, well and good; and if not, you shall be killed by this sword. This is what is said: ״אם תאבו ושמעתם טוב הארץ תאכלו״ etc., ״ואם תמאנו ומריתם חרב תאכלו״ etc. — ״כי פי ה׳ דבר״. And where did He speak? At the time of the giving of the Torah He stipulated this with them. And this is what the liturgist composed in the azharot: ״ראשית עטיפת הזיין צהלה ורנה״."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:31.935717283Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}